### REQ-06 Configuration under control

- **Objective:** the tool configuration that governs behaviour (managed or admin settings, permission mode, allow / deny rules, sandbox, hooks, MCP or extension allow-list, instruction files) is baselined with hashes, changed only through change control, and cannot be overridden by users.
- **Acceptance:** baseline captured and hashed (`python3 checks/capture_baseline.py`, IQ-03) and recorded in {{doc_id_06}}; version recorded per surface (IQ-01); a user-level attempt to override a managed setting has no effect (OQ-09); instruction and configuration files in repositories require code-owner review.
{{#is_claude_code}}
- **Claude Code:** managed settings (system `managed-settings.json`, MDM, or server-managed from the admin console) take precedence over `--settings`, `.claude/settings.local.json`, `.claude/settings.json` and `~/.claude/settings.json`. Candidate locks: `permissions.disableBypassPermissionsMode` = `"disable"`; `disableAutoMode` = `"disable"` or an explicit managed `permissions.defaultMode`; `allowManagedPermissionRulesOnly`; `allowManagedHooksOnly` (CI and agent runners) or, on developer machines, `pluginConfigs` `cc-plugin-sec-default@builtin` option `allowManagedModsOnly` with `disableSideloadFlags`; `allowManagedMcpServersOnly`; `availableModels` with `availableModelsMatch` = `"exact"` and `enforceAvailableModels`. `CLAUDE.md` is guidance for the model. Verify the effective sources with `/status` ("Setting sources") and `claude doctor`. Server-managed settings are a client-side control only; endpoint-managed settings give stronger guarantees.
{{/is_claude_code}}
{{#is_codex}}
- **Codex:** admin-enforced `requirements.toml` (`/etc/codex/requirements.toml`, Windows `%ProgramData%\OpenAI\Codex\requirements.toml`, macOS MDM, or cloud-managed requirements); a conflicting user value falls back to an allowed value with a notice. Candidate keys: `allowed_approval_policies`, `allowed_sandbox_modes` or `allowed_permission_profiles`, `allow_managed_hooks_only`, `[mcp_servers]` identity allow-list, `[rules]` with `prompt` or `forbidden` decisions, `allowed_approvals_reviewers = ["user"]`. `managed_config.toml` only supplies startup defaults that users can change during a run. Project `.codex/config.toml` loads only for trusted projects.
{{/is_codex}}
{{#is_copilot}}
- **GitHub Copilot:** enterprise and organisation policies (capture dated screenshots; no REST export was verified), repository instruction files (`.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `.github/instructions/`, `AGENTS.md`) and hooks (`.github/hooks/`). Copilot code review reads instructions from the PR head branch, so protect these files with CODEOWNERS and required code-owner review. Set the "Default policy for new features" and "Default availability for released models" policies explicitly so that new features and models are not enabled outside change control.
{{/is_copilot}}
{{#is_cursor}}
- **Cursor:** team or enterprise admin settings (Privacy Mode enforced, Run Mode policy, model and MCP allow / block lists), Team Rules, project `.cursor/rules`, `.cursor/BUGBOT.md`, hooks. Cursor describes terminal and MCP allow-lists as best-effort guardrails.
{{/is_cursor}}
