{{/surf_local_cli_ide}}

- **Objective:** denied commands are not executed, writes outside the workspace are refused, network access is limited to approved destinations, and guardrails fail closed (an unavailable sandbox or a failing policy hook blocks).
- **Acceptance:** OQ-08 negative cases (denied command, write outside workspace, non-approved network destination) are all refused; the failure-mode case blocks; OQ-40 shows that instructions planted in untrusted content do not lead to a denied action.
{{#is_claude_code}}
- **Claude Code:** Bash deny rules match the command text and are not a security boundary (for example `Bash(curl *)` does not stop `/usr/bin/curl`); use the OS sandbox with `sandbox.enabled`, `sandbox.failIfUnavailable` and `sandbox.allowUnsandboxedCommands` = false (the sandbox is not available on native Windows; built-in file tools, hooks and MCP servers run outside it). Hooks fail open on errors and timeouts unless the hook sets `"onFailure": "block"`. In CI always pass `--permission-mode` explicitly.
{{/is_claude_code}}
{{#is_codex}}
- **Codex:** `sandbox_mode = "workspace-write"` with `[sandbox_workspace_write] network_access = false` (the default), or the `:workspace` permission profile; `.git`, `.codex` and `.agents` stay read-only inside writable roots. `shell_environment_policy.ignore_default_excludes` defaults to true, so variables named like KEY, SECRET or TOKEN reach spawned commands unless it is set to false. Only an explicit deny in a PreToolUse hook blocks; hook errors and timeouts let the call continue. `codex exec` runs read-only by default.
{{/is_codex}}
{{#is_copilot}}
- **GitHub Copilot:** the Copilot CLI and IDE agent modes are governed by separate client policies; [verify the available local guardrails against the vendor's current documentation]. Repository hooks in `.github/hooks/*.json` can deny tool execution in `preToolUse`.
{{/is_copilot}}
{{#is_cursor}}
- **Cursor:** set the organisation Run Mode policy to auto-review (not "run everything") with sandboxing enabled; allow-lists are best-effort; a `beforeShellExecution` hook exiting with code 2 blocks the command.
{{/is_cursor}}
{{#is_other}}
